<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy selling up to 3.75 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy selling up to 3.75 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it was offering to sell up to 3.75 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT) expiring between January 31, 1997 and March 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Bids must be received by 1030 GMT.</p>
</text>
